  "body": "Adds a Synthetos TinyG post and a generic 3-axis router/mill so CamCraft can produce TinyG programs with manual tool changes, expanded drilling and explicit refusals for unsupported operations.\n\nStacked on #715 (grblHAL), integrated through `c9822758`; main integrated through `37482923`. The original branch includes release tag `v0.16.0`.\n\nThe compatibility update stops spindle and coolant before manual changes, restores a safe Z height after M0, refuses feeds that would format as F0, splits XY arcs into at most half turns, and linearizes non-XY arcs within a 0.005 mm bound including rounding. An optional script-level spindle dwell follows M3; smoothing requests produce one explanatory comment without inventing a controller tolerance word.\n\nThe merge keeps main's post/machine registrations and Heidenhain stream behavior. Contour lead goldens were regenerated for main's CAM geometry changes. The latest #715 parent already contains the corresponding grblHAL golden updates.\n\nEvidence and validation:\n\n- Final commit `572c6ed884546befcd6693e2a7681b006844b735` matches the tested working tree. TinyG-focused checks: **88 tests passed**, and `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test tinyg_post --test coolant --test conformance`: TinyG 18/18, coolant 7/7 and conformance 6/6 passed.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-post --test script_tinyg --test comp`: script cases 11/11 and compensation cases 9/9 passed.\n- Final affected app suites: conformance 6, control compensation 5, coolant follow-ups 7, Fanuc cross-post checks 12, inverted-post checks 15, TinyG 18, wear compensation 5; plus the 20 post-script/compensation tests above.\n- The repository-wide quick gate is **not claimed green**: it found the inherited grblHAL post is missing its required recorded suite (`recorded_streams::every_shipped_post_script_has_its_suite`). That broader run was stopped. This TinyG revision does not add grblHAL tests or fixes; the parent-suite gap remains separately identified.\n- Regression coverage includes `feeds_that_round_to_zero_are_refused_in_each_machine_unit`, `full_xy_circles_and_helices_split_without_losing_direction_or_depth`, `vertical_arcs_are_chords_within_five_microns`, `first_cut_after_a_tool_change_seats_at_a_safe_start_height`, and `spindle_delay_is_optional_validated_and_rounds_up_in_seconds`.\n- Final 13 conformance TinyG goldens replayed through the existing edge-next host executable: 759 lines, 1,566 planner blocks; zero failures, refusals, alarms or findings. The executable records dirty firmware source at `998c02eb`; CPS SHA-256 `99905fc06fb604b7ddbb3d119f60cdc50bdfe52bd6190500bb12752168c2ae4c`. The six runnable script-suite goldens also pass: 254 lines and 369 blocks; five named-refusal snapshots are not controller programs. Combined: 19 programs, 1,013 lines and 1,935 blocks, all clean.\n- Independent mocked geometry screen: 32 non-XY helical-arc cases across mm/inch, XZ/YZ, CW/CCW and radii 0.01/1/10/100 mm; maximum sampled chord radial deviation 0.004871692 mm. This is a mathematical screen, not a stock-clearance or hardware proof.\n- Behavior basis: public TinyG documentation and a user-supplied behavior review of master 440.21 and edge-next 450.x. No GPL firmware source was consulted by the CamCraft implementation agents.\n- Master runtime verification was attempted, but the existing host adapters are incompatible with that revision. No independent master replay or physical-board verification is claimed.\n- Host replay does not simulate operator jogging, physical stepping, spindle acceleration, serial flow, or real feedhold timing. Senders must hold streaming at M0 when the operator changes offsets. Short-segment simplification and a Setup UI for the script-level spindle-wait option are outside this PR.\n\nChangelog: Add a TinyG 3-axis post with manual tool changes, expanded drilling, bounded arc output, feed-rounding refusals and an optional script-level spindle-start dwell.\n\nFixes #836\n",
